<http://data.silknow.org/object/b7092b03-99c7-38e1-ad1b-cbff96427515/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Woven coral pink silk damask panel, brocaded in gold and silver. It is made up from several pieces of the same material, and has a border of silver braid all round. It is lined with bright yellow taffetta. The material has a semi-bizarre design in gold and silver thread composed of curling scrolls and exotic fruit. The main details of the design are echoed in the damask pattern. There are at least 3 repeats in the width of the material.  \n\n<u>Technical details</u> \nTissue, with damask ground based on a satin of 5. The brocaded metal wefts are used in pairs (file). The gold thread is made from a silver strip wound on a yellow silk core. The silver thread is wound on a white silk core. The brocaded wefts are bound in 3/1 twill. The binding warp is taken from the ground."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/b7092b03-99c7-38e1-ad1b-cbff96427515> .

<http://data.silknow.org/vam>
        ecrm:P106_is_composed_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/7fc6219f-c852-342d-ba5b-facee7e21fde> .

